"]],["basis","NOUN","","",["pobj","as"]],["for","ADP","","",["prep","basis"]],["the","DET","","",["det","evaluation"]],["normative","ADJ","","",["amod","evaluation"]],["evaluation","NOUN","","",["pobj","for"]],["and","CCONJ","","",["cc","evaluation"]],["guidance","NOUN","","",["conj","evaluation"]],["of","ADP","","",["prep","evaluation"]],["AI","PROPN","","ORG",["compound","technology"]],["technologies","NOUN","technology","",["pobj","of"]],"",["referring","VERB","refer","",["advcl","consider"]],["to","ADP","","",["prep","refer"]],["human","ADJ","","",["amod","dignity"]],["dignity","NOUN","","",["pobj","to"],[1.7,""]],"",["well","ADV","","",["compound","being"],[1.1,""]],"",["being","NOUN","","",["npadvmod","refer"]],["and","CCONJ","","",["cc","being"]],["the","DET","","",["det","prevention"]],["prevention","NOUN","","",["conj","being"]],["of","ADP","","",["prep","prevention"]],["harm","NOUN","","",["pobj","of"],[-2.5,""]],["as","ADP","","",["prep","prevention"]],["a","DET","","",["det","compass"]],["compass","NOUN","","",["pobj","as"]],["and","CCONJ","","",["cc","as"]],["as","SCONJ","","",["mark","root"]],["rooted","VERB","root","",["conj","as"]],["in","ADP","","",["prep","root"]],["the","DET","","",["det","ethic"]],["ethics","NOUN","ethic","",["pobj","in"]],["of","ADP","","",["prep","ethic"]],["science","NOUN","","",["pobj","of"]],["and","CCONJ","","",["cc","science"]],["technology","NOUN","","",["conj","science"]],""],"neg=0.035,neu=0.805,pos=0.16,compound=0.5828"],[["neg=0.0,neu=0.0,pos=0.0,compound=0.0,span=This Recommendation does not have the ambition to provide one single definition of AI, since such a definition would need to change over time, in accordance with technological developments.","neg=0.0,neu=0.845,pos=0.155,compound=0.5106,span=Rather, its ambition is to address those features of AI systems that are of central ethical relevance.","neg=0.0,neu=0.933,pos=0.067,compound=0.4588,span=Therefore, this Recommendation approaches AI systems as systems which have the capacity to process data and information in a way that resembles intelligent behaviour, and typically includes aspects of reasoning, learning, perception, prediction, planning or control.","neg=0.0,neu=0.0,pos=0.0,compound=0.0,span=Three elements have a central place in this approach:","neg=0.0,neu=0.0,pos=0.0,compound=0.0,span=AI systems are information-processing technologies that integrate models and algorithms that produce a capacity to learn and to perform cognitive tasks leading to outcomes such as prediction and decision-making in material and virtual environments.","neg=0.104,neu=0.896,pos=0.0,compound=-0.4404,span=AI systems are designed to operate with varying degrees of autonomy by means of knowledge modelling and representation and by exploiting data and calculating correlations.","neg=0.0,neu=0.924,pos=0.076,compound=0.2808,span=AI systems may include several methods, such as but not limited to:machine learning, including deep learning and reinforcement learning;machine reasoning, including planning, scheduling, knowledge representation and reasoning, search, and optimization.","neg=0.0,neu=0.0,pos=0.0,compound=0.0,span=AI systems can be used in cyber-physical systems, including the Internet of things, robotic systems, social robotics, and human-computer interfaces, which involve control, perception, the processing of data collected by sensors, and the operation of actuators in the environment in which AI systems work.","neg=0.0,neu=0.943,pos=0.057,compound=0.5106,span=Ethical questions regarding AI systems pertain to all stages of the AI system life cycle, understood here to range from research, design and development to deployment and use, including maintenance, operation, trade, financing, monitoring and evaluation, validation, end-of-use, disassembly and termination.","neg=0.0,neu=0.938,pos=0.062,compound=0.4588,span=In addition, AI actors can be defined as any actor involved in at least one stage of the AI system life cycle, and can refer both to natural and legal persons, such as researchers, programmers, engineers, data scientists, end-users, business enterprises, universities and public and private entities, among others.","neg=0.0,neu=0.87,pos=0.13,compound=0.8168,span=AI systems raise new types of ethical issues that include, but are not limited to, their impact on decision-making, employment and labour, social interaction, health care, education, media, access to information, digital divide, personal data and consumer protection, environment, democracy, rule of law, security and policing, dual use, and human rights and fundamental freedoms, including freedom of expression, privacy and non- discrimination.","neg=0.083,neu=0.752,pos=0.165,compound=0.3182,span=Furthermore, new ethical challenges are created by the potential of AI algorithms to reproduce and reinforce existing biases, and thus to exacerbate already existing forms of discrimination, prejudice and stereotyping.","neg=0.051,neu=0.949,pos=0.0,compound=-0.2263,span=Some of these issues are related to the capacity of AI systems to perform tasks which previously only living beings could do, and which were in some cases even limited to human beings only.","neg=0.0,neu=0.934,pos=0.066,compound=0.5106,span=These characteristics give AI systems a profound, new role in human practices and society, as well as in their relationship with the environment and ecosystems, creating a new context for children and young people to grow up in, develop an understanding of the world and themselves, critically understand media and information, and learn to make decisions.","neg=0.0,neu=0.827,pos=0.173,compound=0.765,span=In the long term, AI systems could challenge humans’ special sense of experience and agency, raising additional concerns about, inter alia, human self- understanding, social, cultural and environmental interaction, autonomy, agency, worth and dignity."],["This Recommendation","the ambition","one single definition","AI","such a definition","time","accordance","technological developments","its ambition","those features","AI systems","that","central ethical relevance","AI systems","systems","which","the capacity","data","information","a way","that","intelligent behaviour","aspects","reasoning","learning","perception","prediction","planning","control","Three elements","a central place","this approach","AI systems","information-processing technologies","that","models","algorithms","that","a capacity","cognitive tasks","outcomes","prediction","decision-making","material","virtual environments","AI systems","varying degrees","autonomy","means","knowledge modelling","representation","data","correlations","AI systems","several methods","machine learning","deep learning","reinforcement","reasoning","planning","scheduling","knowledge representation","reasoning","search","optimization","AI systems","cyber-physical systems","the Internet","things","robotic systems","social robotics","human-computer interfaces","which","control","perception","the processing","data","sensors","the operation","actuators","the environment","which","Ethical questions","AI systems","all stages","the AI system life cycle","research","design","development","deployment","use","maintenance","operation","trade","financing","monitoring","evaluation","validation","end","use","disassembly","termination","addition","AI actors","any actor","at least one stage","the AI system life cycle","both","natural and legal persons","researchers","programmers","engineers","data scientists","end-users","business enterprises","universities","public and private entities","others","AI systems","new types","ethical issues","that","their impact","employment","labour","social interaction","health care","education","media","access","information","digital divide","personal data","consumer protection","environment","democracy","rule","law","security","policing","dual use","human rights","fundamental freedoms","freedom","expression","privacy","non- discrimination","new ethical challenges","the potential","AI algorithms","existing biases","already existing forms","discrimination","prejudice","Some","these issues","the capacity","AI systems","tasks","which","only living beings","which","some cases","human beings","These characteristics","AI systems","a profound, new role","human practices","society","their relationship","the environment","ecosystems","a new context","children","young people","an understanding","the world","themselves","media","information","decisions","the long term","AI systems","humans","special sense","experience","agency","additional concerns","inter alia","human self- understanding","social, cultural and environmental interaction","autonomy","agency","dignity"],[["This","DET","this","",["det","Recommendation"]],["Recommendation","PROPN","","ORG",["nsubj","have"]],["does","AUX","do","",["aux","have"]],["not","PART","","",["neg","have"]],["have","VERB","","",["ROOT","have"]],["the","DET","","",["det","ambition"]],["ambition","NOUN","","",["dobj","have"]],["to","PART","","",["aux","provide"]],["provide","VERB","","",["acl","ambition"]],["one","NUM","","CARDINAL",["nummod","definition"]],["single","ADJ","","",["amod","definition"]],["definition","NOUN","","",["dobj","provide"]],["of","ADP","","",["prep","definition"]],["AI","PROPN","","ORG",["pobj","of"]],"",["since","SCONJ","","",["mark","need"]],["such","DET","","",["predet","definition"]],["a","DET","","",["det","definition"]],["definition","NOUN","","",["nsubj","need"]],["would","AUX","","",["aux","need"]],["need","VERB","","",["advcl","have"]],["to","PART","","",["aux","change"]],["change","VERB","","",["xcomp","need"]],["over","ADP","","",["prep","change"]],["time","NOUN","","",["pobj","over"]],"",["in","ADP","","",["prep","need"]],["accordance","NOUN","","",["pobj","in"]],["with","ADP","","",["prep","accordance"]],["technological","ADJ","","",["amod","development"]],["developments","NOUN","development","",["pobj","with"]],"",["Rather","ADV","rather","",[